      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Minneapolis & St. Louis Railroad reached the area in 1877, sparking Norwegian settlement and the town’s early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://newrichlandmn.gov/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1902 New Richland Odd Fellows Hall, also known as “Stranger’s Refuge,” is the city’s sole National Register of Historic Places listing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
